# aicomply is a DLP / content-normalization library. Its normalization tests,
# benchmark corpus + generator, and documentation MUST contain invisible-unicode
# and homoglyph characters as fixtures and worked examples -- those characters
# are the very inputs the normalize layer exists to fold (NFKC, zero-width strip,
# homoglyph fold). HackMyAgent's UNICODE-STEGO-001 / UNICODE-STEGO-005 checks
# fire on these intentional samples. This is the same situation HMA documents in
# its own .hmaignore ("scanner contains the detection patterns that match the
# threats it detects").
#
# Suppression is path-scoped, not a global check-ID disable, so UNICODE-STEGO
# still fires on any NEW source file outside these intentional-fixture paths.

# Normalization unit-test fixtures: zero-width, full-width, and homoglyph samples by design
src/normalize/__tests__/
src/classifier/dual-layer/__tests__/dual-layer-normalize.test.ts
python/tests/test_normalize.py

# Adversarial accuracy corpus + its generator: intentionally evasion-shaped inputs
bench/

# Docs demonstrate the invisible-unicode / homoglyph attack with literal examples
# (e.g. the README audit-trail example normalizes full-width digits to ASCII)
README.md
SECURITY.md
